    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup for **Ghost Ride the WHIP** is anchored by a high-upside trio of starters who are primed to capitalize on favorable pitching matchups. **Corbin Carroll** (73.39) and **Vinnie Pasquantino** (72.92) headline the card; **Corbin Carroll** benefits from a strong lineup position and a favorable dynamic platoon split, while **Vinnie Pasquantino** is the day\u2019s premier value, taking advantage of a high xERA (5.31) from his opponent to maximize his base projection. **Seiya Suzuki** (65.61) rounds out our elite-tier starts, carrying significant momentum into a matchup against a pitcher with a 4.27 xERA, where his ability to exploit a slow delivery creates a valuable stolen base opportunity\u2014a critical factor given our aggressive pursuit of the scarcest category.\n\nWe remain cautious regarding potential volatility in the bottom half of the order, specifically with **Mickey Moniak** (49.11) and **Zach McKinstry** (47.86), whose scores are hampered by unfavorable platoons and difficult matchups against elite hold pitchers. **Isaac Paredes** (60.65) and **Brice Turang** (60.44) provide reliable stability in the infield, with **Isaac Paredes** bolstered by a solid 9% dynamic platoon edge. Our most difficult bench decision involved **Austin Riley** (42.28); while he possesses high raw talent, he fell just short of our 40.0 efficiency floor due to a suppressive matchup against a 3.01 xERA starter, ultimately losing out to the more favorable platoon advantages held by **Josh Naylor** and **Gabriel Moreno**. We are closely monitoring lineup confirmations for **Gabriel Moreno**, **Max Muncy**, **Travis Bazzana**, **Corbin Carroll**, **Seiya Suzuki**, and **Josh Naylor**, as any significant downward shift in batting order could further compress these efficiency scores. Finally, we continue to carry **James Wood** on the IL, awaiting his return to bolster our outfield depth alongside bench assets like **Griffin Conine**, **Cole Young**, **Trevor Story**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Edwin Arroyo**, and **Henry Bolte**.",
